+# Cache eviction
+
+Muninn does not implement a cache/memory eviction policy of its own: compression
+and eviction of accumulated memory is recorded as delegated to existing,
+externally measured systems rather than built in-project. The recorded basis is
+MemForest (arXiv:2609.08273), which partitions memory into EventTrees with
+progressive fusion and, under Mem0, retains 97.1% of performance while
+compressing 50% of history with a 1.89x retrieval speedup (99.7% retention at
+50% compression and 2.24x speedup under M3-Agent); the project's conclusion from
+this evidence is explicit: "La compresión y el desalojo son un problema resuelto
+por otros y medido. Se delega" (compression and eviction are a problem already
+solved by others and measured — it is delegated) [N3].
